Orchestrator-directed fixes applied to pipeline/acquire.py, effective at the
next chunk boundary (this chunk, years 2016-2020, is already running with
the previous flow-year-scoped-revert code in memory and will finish under
it; do not touch 2013-2015 raw files, already valid evidence):
1. Three-level cascade per flow-year: 25-chapter batches (180s) first;
   on the FIRST failure, escalate to 10-chapter batches (180s) for the
   rest of that flow-year (not two failures at 25, since exports has
   shown consistent, not intermittent, failure at size 25); at size 10,
   a single failure gets immediate per-chapter fill without abandoning
   size 10, and two CONSECUTIVE size-10 failures abandon size 10 for the
   remainder, going straight to per-chapter (60s). Every flow-year starts
   fresh at level 1.
2. hs2_completeness now reports complete based solely on the partner-code
   set matching partner_totals (CONTRACT's own completeness proof), not
   on every individual request returning 200 (a legitimate 204 for a
   chapter with no data, e.g. chapter 99 on exports, is not an
   incompleteness). Log lines changed from "hs2 incomplete ... missing 0
   codes" (misleading; the removed all_batches_ok check was counting
   normal 204 responses in the per-chapter fallback as failures) to
   "hs2 complete for <flow> <year>: strategy=<...>, rows=<...>,
   partner_codes=<...>" when the code sets match, "hs2 INCOMPLETE ..."
   only when they genuinely do not.
