Second orchestrator-directed fix, effective at the next chunk boundary
(years 2021-2025; the current chunk, 2016-2020, keeps running under the
25/10/per-chapter ladder code already in memory, sequential per-chapter,
no concurrency): once level 2 (10-chapter batches) has failed at least
once for a flow-year, subsequent per-chapter (level 3) requests for that
SAME flow-year run with concurrency 2 (two in flight, each its own
independently 0.5s-paced CensusClient instance writing to the same
raw/<id>/hs2/ directory, same 180s timeout, same bounded retries, never
more than two). Any HTTP 429 or 5xx observed under concurrency is logged
as a concurrent failure; after two such failures in a flow-year,
concurrency drops back to 1 (sequential, 60s timeout) for the rest of
that flow-year. File names and part numbering are unchanged (each chapter
still gets its own sequential part number, assigned before dispatch so
there is no race). hs2_completeness and file evidence for already-saved
years are untouched.
