chapter (98 requests per member-month-flow, about 14 min each, projected
about 3 hours for all 14 month-flows) to one request per member-month-flow
with CTY_CODE pinned to the single member code, COMM_LVL=HS2, and no
commodity predicate, which returns every chapter for that partner in one
response (the same shape proven in source test item 5 for China, 98 rows
in one call). Killed the in-flight per-chapter run (pid 45117) after 4
month-flows had already completed fully per-chapter (exports 4791
2013-07, exports 4791 2013-08, imports 4791 2013-07, imports 4791
2013-08, all 98/98 files) and one was partial (imports 4791 2013-09, 43
files, discarded and refetched fresh); those 4 completed month-flows are
kept as valid per-chapter evidence, unchanged. pipeline/build.py's
RawArchive.eu_member_month_hs2 reads either form (single consolidated
file or per-chapter parts), cached per month-flow. Remaining month-flows
use the single-request form, falling back to per-chapter only if the
single request fails.
